hits.text:
a few days ago we published the "No AI Slop Manifesto" at @aiDotEngineer Code Summit in SF, written in collaboration with many of the speakers and attendees

It already hit the front page of hacker news, has 300+ signatures including folks from Baseten, SpaceX, OpenAI, PostHog, Shopify, Glean, ZoomInfo, and legendary builders including 

@swyx 
@poteto 
@kentcdodds 
@mihail_eric 
@audreyt  
@altryne 
@traviscline 
@philipkiely 
@TejasKumar_

read and sign it at slopmanifesto dot com

some of my favorite points 

> AI cannot replace human judgement, it can only amplify our judgement (or lack thereof).

> We own the intent, taste, and consequences of what we ship, however much AI helps us make it.

> There will always be alpha in reviewing *something*. As models improve, we may stop reading most of the code. We may still review a plan, design, or result, because if we don't, we just get the same output as everyone else.

